{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0e5d29b6dedc005b653821275afa67ebd02afd880a6eb405e5eb7a196615fc8c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"jigjoy-ai/baro@f9a610774532 snapshot a7f091ec4bf6f132","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_bfef82491b37f41a283d7c23086735b3e96c17cc311a7ab3046838036c75b3c2","slc_dd91b5a36e911747be1671e0f407c8043cbc89ec12f6829104c5551eeea51ffd"],"source_ids":["src_9a5c51749a775bd7908166914ee6d87e"],"text":"Repository development practice: the experiment guide instructs preparing a clean git repo with an unexecuted prd.json whose stories have concrete acceptance criteria and test commands, and installing workspace dependencies with npm install before running trials.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_105014d924b25e519cecc21d417b0d2de15a7cdb764de15ab0c6e84752a8697f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"jigjoy-ai/baro@f9a610774532 snapshot a7f091ec4bf6f132","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0dbd8de84705cd94922d72afa5abc6b5610b2f97e72502176cbd08e689cfd76c","slc_c56e113c2a19061005bb110ebe49af039d01327818ee1ba21752ad3fd479806b"],"source_ids":["src_9a5c51749a775bd7908166914ee6d87e","src_ddc01746f1165a62b36cb7b76b0fa1cc"],"text":"`--local-only` disables pushes and PRs but is explicitly not an OS or network sandbox, since story agents can execute arbitrary shell commands; a hard no-push boundary requires removing git remotes.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1a78f2e24d029f64423c450abc8fb39f316d40b40233281a4d59ed951fb7e376","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"jigjoy-ai/baro@f9a610774532 snapshot a7f091ec4bf6f132","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_662e07efc11f5c5abd0d003727a1e6e39e4626268018ef3eb760bb590ba3557a","slc_ae87d5fc8640a00033bf1fee85c290f27d08dc21d425869ef73b8731a11d93c4"],"source_ids":["src_ddc01746f1165a62b36cb7b76b0fa1cc"],"text":"Merges are blocked behind fail-closed gates: declared tests, build-before-commit, an evidence critic judging captured command output, and write-surface ownership; the human reviews a PR the gates already accepted.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_31d494bd46599975f396e273b9c161237a5e8067e2bb73f2ce4cd14613a801eb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=relevance","setting":"jigjoy-ai/baro@f9a610774532 snapshot a7f091ec4bf6f132","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3e152f18d0963f51c7edd3c7465c18d2c62c93f1d3cb110d5c8b00f27a703502"],"source_ids":["src_ddc01746f1165a62b36cb7b76b0fa1cc"],"text":"A cloud option runs the same fleet on a hosted site with isolated sandboxes and provider keys, or users can attach their own machine as a cloud runner via `baro login` and `baro connect --install-service`.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3d6a7d0597e6ca15591c35cdbf4113cdb7106ddda2212e97034005af8fda2239","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"jigjoy-ai/baro@f9a610774532 snapshot a7f091ec4bf6f132","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2c4f64602749c880523b7dd64985b44234c400e430e4586a08840b7c83b5d881","slc_e6fe9f4eb4ce38c646b4b12d4d34f77a07f6daef934af062edb927dead15705a"],"source_ids":["src_3e20a7f65eef5c579ad41eddb06e0f40","src_9a5c51749a775bd7908166914ee6d87e"],"text":"Codex, OpenCode, and Pi workers are one-shot CLI processes that cannot consume corrective messages after exit; failed verdicts for those backends require a separate recovery execution rather than in-process revision.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_51bb064a0be450abf3833e9edcf1095eeac19fcfd26d96861f34fe203ab43cfe","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"jigjoy-ai/baro@f9a610774532 snapshot a7f091ec4bf6f132","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1b83cb6b8facc3914581a746d5644e1455cdc685bc83fc00a68575c8857ba45f","slc_5c4dd57c5df6d0e1cbc1d317cea83cc755a305389cb736eb6c4cb868b25a6efe"],"source_ids":["src_9a5c51749a775bd7908166914ee6d87e"],"text":"Collective coordination is the CLI default; a legacy Conductor mode (one owner of DAG levels, retries, completion) can be selected with `--coordination legacy` for A/B comparison.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_630a3eb1b0633aa3bc1604d67ebf3a855db38c1a79fa35bfc09e1a9b75b7e73c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"jigjoy-ai/baro@f9a610774532 snapshot a7f091ec4bf6f132","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_53030689d1df9ad77ddd431c81be4532239c3b0c4a387b25b9ab6f48f1f1521a"],"source_ids":["src_3e20a7f65eef5c579ad41eddb06e0f40"],"text":"The runtime is distributed but not leaderless: the Board serializes scheduling and durable graph commits while separate participants own goal meaning, route selection, lease granting, quality evaluation, merging, and verification.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6e0cee3d0ef9fb48d2a64af69932471fa3a2d75b324d2a606248af898c4b840f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"jigjoy-ai/baro@f9a610774532 snapshot a7f091ec4bf6f132","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_06fec732226659c52339156c5c61e151d72d99bf68ce96abed66dd1859229589"],"source_ids":["src_9a5c51749a775bd7908166914ee6d87e"],"text":"Runtime replan proposals carry run/story/lease/generation and a graphVersion; invalid, stale, cyclic, unauthorized, over-budget or non-durable candidates get a correlated rejection and are never shown as applied just because a model requested them.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_766911624b7300063f436a3c324000b42f9c0aee1fb1362034b1a4ca01d22eb9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"jigjoy-ai/baro@f9a610774532 snapshot a7f091ec4bf6f132","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_dd7472e3865d3e2627d037be93f0cb650c62d8c00c061a55a488879457efe262"],"source_ids":["src_ddc01746f1165a62b36cb7b76b0fa1cc"],"text":"The tool requires Node 20+, git, and at least one LLM backend: the claude CLI (default), codex, or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint; `baro --doctor` checks the setup.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_92d2d411d0709701e7fd56b0da87655c88254493c97f754d78e2ff67f56fa2c1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"jigjoy-ai/baro@f9a610774532 snapshot a7f091ec4bf6f132","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0dbd8de84705cd94922d72afa5abc6b5610b2f97e72502176cbd08e689cfd76c"],"source_ids":["src_ddc01746f1165a62b36cb7b76b0fa1cc"],"text":"Flags include backend selection (--llm claude|codex|openai|opencode|pi|hybrid|jigjoy), model override, effort level, parallel agent count, execution mode, --quick, --local-only, per-command shell budget, custom OpenAI base URL, and per-tier backend mapping.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9de5bb01170e5a33f41495cc23c00132ee1f87e71bca99c5775edf62c83a7fa6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"jigjoy-ai/baro@f9a610774532 snapshot a7f091ec4bf6f132","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_732b4135da596c72e2bb1c5651557fef0a5d8086d0d136536640b85670b29fe5"],"source_ids":["src_9a5c51749a775bd7908166914ee6d87e"],"text":"The public CLI does not yet expose process-level run resumption: a restart creates a new run identity, keeps the graph version as baseline, resets the discovery budget, and does not expose the old decision ledger.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a3e7704c988709fe7a6c2df6530d7718a051a5dbe007aee06cf28061a80d8ca2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"jigjoy-ai/baro@f9a610774532 snapshot a7f091ec4bf6f132","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_29241bfba71b637c4134edad80f0465a107b8ecf4bf48272644317e8754a4ce8","slc_a596ed41d1d3a1a49fd47ea2bb3c861c6fade7f5476881fa8f04d1e649013b34"],"source_ids":["src_ddc01746f1165a62b36cb7b76b0fa1cc"],"text":"CLI commands include headless detached runs printing a run id, `watch` and `logs` for following runs, `runs`/`stop` for listing and stopping, `--resume` (never re-plans), `--continue` (always re-plans), `--doctor`, `login`, and `connect`.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_aad8c4d7e94fad5ffbc9d4e4979621a34a4ed639df0fb167335c949fc0a86df1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"jigjoy-ai/baro@f9a610774532 snapshot a7f091ec4bf6f132","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_16799e482e43cb26917ad5ce89583509067d403aa3c98769fa6fa9c5cf6e1e76","slc_23b9c216074e5d7ae97725eebcaf92a0913d55a4ccaeb7f509753ef8e45b86c2","slc_46d3c66b3113a2de6dda2b2c9a37c37d1b91bb7e6b826435584c66d42f5120b8","slc_cc929d56349d4531eaee08d5bdde30a4a6635739bd0db24484f48fa50505af3b","slc_e643fcee23b878b50f7d12955a06ac4ce45f951b3e364a5213543caacd2a0c76"],"source_ids":["src_9a5c51749a775bd7908166914ee6d87e"],"text":"A paired A/B harness (ab-run.ts) compares legacy vs collective coordination on identical PRD bytes across isolated clones, alternating arm order, hashing verify inputs, and producing per-trial artifacts including diff.patch, metrics.json, and audit logs.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ac7cfaff3f1e8029288f36cb28451ce63f696ff44703e632c0749bbe48f91958","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"jigjoy-ai/baro@f9a610774532 snapshot a7f091ec4bf6f132","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_826e5ab814899292fbc988d977c838373b712f0eea2138f4076df080a29c9735"],"source_ids":["src_ddc01746f1165a62b36cb7b76b0fa1cc"],"text":"The architecture is described as a Rust TUI host plus a TypeScript orchestrator whose bounded contexts communicate over the Mozaik event bus, with machine gates in front of every merge.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ae96de8fd332dcf0913d4e9163301ad6f790682478413c91bb7fb89f6c980274","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"jigjoy-ai/baro@f9a610774532 snapshot a7f091ec4bf6f132","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1b83cb6b8facc3914581a746d5644e1455cdc685bc83fc00a68575c8857ba45f"],"source_ids":["src_9a5c51749a775bd7908166914ee6d87e"],"text":"In collective mode, workers publish credential-free capabilities and bids, a broker grants a correlated lease to a deterministic winner, and with the Critic enabled a story passes only after the acceptance verdict plus StoryMerged, not merely when the model process exits.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_baf49f898612c0d1607a2c499df6a0570704e54eef91703f124b0acef7b75aee","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"jigjoy-ai/baro@f9a610774532 snapshot a7f091ec4bf6f132","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_732b4135da596c72e2bb1c5651557fef0a5d8086d0d136536640b85670b29fe5"],"source_ids":["src_9a5c51749a775bd7908166914ee6d87e"],"text":"Proposal IDs act as idempotency keys: exact re-delivery returns the remembered decision without reapplying, reuse with different content is rejected, and applied decisions can be restored from the PRD's runtimeGraph metadata when a host resumes the same runId.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_bb94c90bc24882cf73f385ce667a79ed9663f7f19767f5a5e236628239cba494","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"jigjoy-ai/baro@f9a610774532 snapshot a7f091ec4bf6f132","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_db3cbf9007c267be0d5c1aab7a1533dfc3c2641032302743508d087a7f72fb6f"],"source_ids":["src_3e20a7f65eef5c579ad41eddb06e0f40"],"text":"The docs state Baro lacks a trusted per-story CandidateVerifier that executes new deterministic commands in the active worktree, so genuinely missing or fully stale command evidence stays inconclusive after bounded rechecks.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_cf08c9b4122ad876d30561aec0b4db4e355bcdc6c8d41d32d4170ff510a8fd1e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"jigjoy-ai/baro@f9a610774532 snapshot a7f091ec4bf6f132","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_662e07efc11f5c5abd0d003727a1e6e39e4626268018ef3eb760bb590ba3557a","slc_ae87d5fc8640a00033bf1fee85c290f27d08dc21d425869ef73b8731a11d93c4"],"source_ids":["src_ddc01746f1165a62b36cb7b76b0fa1cc"],"text":"Goals are compiled by an architect into machine-checkable invariants before coding, split into a DAG of stories built in parallel across isolated git worktrees, with runtime replanning able to add and rewire stories mid-run and failed gates spawning remediation stories.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d8d4ea05c10b8183558cf2b2dc435321fb6e914764821698ba41093323fa6efb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"jigjoy-ai/baro@f9a610774532 snapshot a7f091ec4bf6f132","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8cdef795b6d49eca2f8a2419a5df371c62104f4f820242be054b1cae8a69de5c","slc_98676e425d641f00b9ac1628d51c4701af22a0545a6865ebc33832d44d7567b1"],"source_ids":["src_9a5c51749a775bd7908166914ee6d87e"],"text":"The DialogueAgent is text-only with no codebase tools; it may send a bounded targeted message and one add-only delegation proposal of at most two stories, with no authority over removal, rewiring, priority, retries, model, route, lease, or merging.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e6110d9ddb9d49432414558bbe8d4a4dc45ee554c44e9406e2bd440c0298a359","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"jigjoy-ai/baro@f9a610774532 snapshot a7f091ec4bf6f132","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_21815ed8578b8be469a0f12a3417c9b0dd5217014d482438e0d0d323fe35c4b1","slc_4362ce943c03b59801c7c32fa62055afef7ed879d703d30a89ddc0b09f7a0700","slc_ca1991bff186b5e81d1498119ea4fdca8a9624978a77d66d36df98405c1e8e94"],"source_ids":["src_ddc01746f1165a62b36cb7b76b0fa1cc"],"text":"The product is installed globally via npm as baro-ai and is invoked as `baro \"<goal>\"` inside a repository, opening a TUI where intake asks questions, the user confirms the plan, and the run proceeds.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3e0ba543d1cb4d9cbfb8ca48e67acd63"}
